  "description": "The grid_snapshots bucket record, one per session, the latest (5.39; 5.47). It carries the engine's own binary snapshot as base64, the seq the snapshot is of, the grid's geometry and the engine name and version, so a core that restarts — or a VT worker that dies while the core lives — can restore the screen from it. There is no recording_offset: the session record's recording_committed_offset is the one copy, so a second field meaning the same offset cannot drift (F1). engine.name is a string, not a constant: libghostty-vt is the locked engine and vt10x is the fallback. One persisted value: this record is written in the same bbolt write as the session record's recording_last_seq_out, so at every write snapshot_seq equals recording_last_seq_out. Refused: a recording_offset field, a snapshot that is not base64, and an engine without a version.",
  "corpus": [
    "Storage §8.6",
    "decision 5.39",
    "decision 5.47",
    "plan.md §3 C6",
    "5.39 counters = one, aligned"
  ],
